# Triage for incoming pull requests on a busy repository.
#
# What this one shows: **per-question bounds and thresholds doing real work**, and a `require accuracy` floor.
# `accuracy` is checked against ground-truth labels in the states file, so it only applies to questions whose
# states carry a `labels` entry -- here, `area` and `breaking_change`, which come from the merged PR's own
# labels. `risk` has no ground truth and is held to agreement with the teacher instead.
schema pr_triage
version 1
teacher laya
max_state_tokens 128

choice area "Which part of the system does this pull request touch?"
  compiler  "the schema front end, distillation or the conformance gate"
  runtime   "the inference binary, serving or the kernels"
  firmware  "the mcu target and anything built for a board"
  docs      "documentation, examples and the README"
  build     "CI, packaging, release and the installer"

score risk "How risky is merging this without a careful review?"
  "mechanical or generated; a skim is enough"
  "ordinary change to one area"
  "touches calibration, numerics or the artifact format"

noul breaking_change "Does this pull request change a public interface in a way that would break existing callers?"
  false "additive, internal, or a fix that keeps the same interface"
  true  "renames, removes or changes the meaning of a flag, endpoint, field or artifact format"

threshold 0.80
# A wrong `area` just routes the review to the wrong team, which a human fixes in seconds.
threshold area 0.70
# A missed breaking change ships. Escalate unless the artifact is very sure.
threshold breaking_change 0.92

require agreement >= 0.85
require ece <= 0.05
# Ground truth exists for these two, so demand it directly, not just agreement with the teacher.
require area.accuracy >= 0.88
require breaking_change.accuracy >= 0.95
require breaking_change.ece <= 0.03
require risk.mae <= 0.35
